    {
      "id": 201423,
      "name": "Eric R",
      "username": "Eric_R",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/b9bd4f/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2017-08-07T20:09:55.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Nope - from the Repeat section:</p>\n<blockquote>\n\"If a Repeat specifies where to use it, obey those instructions (instead of the normal Range and Target restrictions).\"\n</blockquote>\nand Insatiable Hunger of the Swarm explicitly says \"an adjacent land\". (Thematically, the swarm is moving.) So you ignore normal Range/Targeting.\n<p>But if it were <span class=\"bbcode-s\">The Land Thrashes In Furious Pain</span>Winds of Rust and Atrophy, which simply says \"<strong>Repeat</strong> this Power\", then you'd choose your target again from scratch and could choose to use Shadows of the Dahan - no need to &nbsp;pay Energy; Shadows of the Dahan is a modification to the Power (specifically, its Range), which is kept when the Power is Repeated.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
      "post_number": 6,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:29:55.444Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
